## 1. Core conclusion

The nature of Moutai's adjustment cycle from 2012 to 2016 is a "triple resonance" adjustment** that combines exogenous policy shocks (eight regulations + anti-corruption), high inventory clearance in the industry, and plasticizer trust crisis**. It took about **18-19 months** from the stock price high in 2012-07 to the valuation bottom in 2014-01. The stock price fell the most **about 55%**, and the PE bottomed out to **about 8-9 times** (the lowest in history since Maotai was listed). The recovery mechanism is a four-wheel drive of "**mass consumption supplementary government affairs + volume control and price protection + channel restructuring + wholesale price recovery**". The mid-term wholesale price decline in 2014, volume and price stabilization in 2015, and complete recovery confirmed in 2016; it intervened at the low point of 2014-01 PE 9x and held it until 2017. The stock price return exceeded **4-5 times**, verifying the classic paradigm of "good company × low valuation".

