## 4. Three major reasons for adjustment

### A. Consumption restrictions on three public affairs (eight regulations 2012-12)
- Industry consensus: Before the eight regulations, ** high-end liquor government consumption accounted for 2/3, and Moutai government consumption accounted for 30-40% of sales**
- **Impact method**: Cliff-like (Moutai’s government affairs channel shipments are expected to be cut in half around the Spring Festival in 2013)
- **Duration**: From the eight regulations in 2012-12 to the anti-corruption peak at the end of 2014, the net loss of government consumption was about **2-3 years**

### B. Plasticizer Incident (2012-11)
- 2012-11-19 21st Century Internet exploded that the plasticizer of Jiugui Liquor exceeded the standard; 11-26 Liquor Index -5.7% in a single day; 12-09 The media once again exposed doubts about the plasticizer test data of Moutai Feitian
- **Short-term impact**: The industry's wholesale price fell sharply by 20-30%, and Moutai's wholesale price fell from 2,000 to 1,500.
- **Recovery time**: About **6-9 months** at the brand level (consumer trust will be basically restored in mid-2013)

### C. Anti-corruption and suppression of high-end consumption (2013-)
- Anti-corruption reached its peak in 2013-2014 (Xu Caihou, Zhou Yongkang and other cases)
- Local government Moutai concentrated consumption scene **systematic evaporation**
- **It was not until the second half of 2015** that the wholesale price stopped falling and stabilized due to the relay of mass consumption.

